    "result_text": "All 33 tests pass (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for the create-owner response (and the owner GET response, which the test reads back through).\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only boolean `bulkSignupWarning` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`BulkSignupWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 A small helper that counts owners whose stored `registrationDate` equals today's business-day-adjusted date and returns `true` when that count exceeds 80. This mirrors how `EnsureDailyCapacity` measures \"created that day\", so the bulk-signup warning and the daily-limit rule accumulate over the same day (as the Cp22 test comment notes).\n\n3. **`RespondWithOwnerCreated.java`** and **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 Inject `OwnerRepository`, compute the flag at response time, and set it on the DTO before sending. Placing it in both responders means the value is correct whether the client reads it from the create (201) response or a subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added `@Mapping(target = \"bulkSignupWarning\", ignore = true)` since the flag isn't derivable from the `Owner` entity alone; it's set explicitly by the responder.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests` (fresh create \u2192 `bulkSignupWarning` is `false`) passes, and the full suite (33 tests) is green.",
